  "articleBody": "Many homeowners wonder whether they can tackle parts of a garage conversion on their own or when it is time to bring in an experienced general contractor. While minor aesthetic changes might seem simple, turning an unconditioned shell into a legal, comfortable living area involves major structural and trade requirements.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps:\n- Structural framing changes: Replacing garage doors with framed exterior walls, adding entry doors, or opening load-bearing walls requires verified structural support.\n- Subfloor and foundation elevation: When garage floors sit lower than the main house or need leveling and damp-proofing before finished flooring can be installed.\n- Adding plumbing or heating: Bringing dedicated bathroom rough-ins, water supply, or safe climate control into the space requires licensed trade coordination.\n- Meeting building regulations: Transforming utility space into a habitable bedroom or suite triggers strict rules for ventilation, egress, and insulation.\n\nAbraham Becerra and the HH Remodeling crew provide on-site leadership, managing custom framing, drywall, and finish trim while keeping the job running smoothly. If you are planning a garage transformation in Aurora or the Denver metro area, reach out to HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 for an estimate.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}